{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And his hand is driven.</b> When he comes to bring the axe down on the wood. And its Targum: ״וְתִתְמְרֵיג יְדֵיהּ״ — a term of ״and his hand slipped off״ to bring the blow of the axe down on the wood. ״כִּי שָׁמְטוּ הַבָּקָר״ (II Samuel 6) — Jonathan rendered: ״אֲרֵי מַרְגוּהִי תוֹרַיָּא״." "<b>And the iron slips from the wood.</b> Some of our Sages say the iron slipped from its handle, and some of them say the iron flung a splinter from the wood that was being split, and it flew off and killed (Makkot 7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:39.173441345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}